    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In the previous chapter, the additive effect of an allele was shown to be equal to the deviation of members of the population with the allele from the population mean phenotype. This definition does not change with the addition of loci. Letting $ G_{i} $ represent the conditional mean phenotype of individuals with allele i at the first locus without regard to the other allele at the locus or to the genotype at the second locus, then",
