    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Here, we have subtracted the mean genotypic value and the additive effects, leaving the dominance effect as the only unexplained portion of the conditional mean at the locus. As in the case of additive effects, the mean dominance deviation at each locus is equal to zero.",
      "source_page": 101,
      "printed_page": 81,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter5:p005:b14"
      ],
      "bbox": [
