      "content_sha256": "bec1ffd55ccf662fa45b11e80172d6f361328b3fafc4321b9960cc71f47222ea"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The open-ended equation merely implies that there are many more terms when more than two loci are involved in the expression of a trait. The parameters in this model depend very much upon the genotype frequencies in the population and can change as allele frequencies change (Example 4, Chapter 4). However, the mean value of each type of effect is always equal to zero.",
      "source_page": 102,
      "printed_page": 82,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter5:p006:b11"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        150.0,
